8. Eclypsium, "USBAnywhere" (2019)
   https://eclypsium.com/blog/virtual-media-vulnerability-in-bmc-opens-servers-to-remote-attack/

   Read for context only. It analyses a materially different Supermicro
   virtual-media implementation (a distinct port and packet format, with a
   fixed RC4 key shared across a vendor's BMCs). Nothing about it transfers to
   ASMB8's protocol, and nothing was derived from it. It is cited because a
   reader comparing BMC virtual-media research would otherwise reasonably
   wonder whether it had been used.
